; the stateful scan pattern: reduce over input with epistemic state.
; reduce graph [state...] (fn state triple -> new-state)
; each input element advances the automaton.
; the state IS the epistemic position: what has been seen, what is active.
; 
; used in 12 tantras: viveka-ganana, extract-solve-for, sandhi-kosha,
; sandhi-avastha, emit-triples, count-chain, grade-sparsha, and more.
; 
; this is the ONLY stateful pattern. all other patterns are pure.
; a tantra has at most one scan — it is always the outermost structure.

(kosha scan-accumulate
  (vishesa computation-varga)
  (swarupa transducer)
  (abheda op-reduce morphism)
  (yukta fold map)
  (janya sequence)
  (phala state)
  (sthita domain-computation))
